---
name: Synchronize a domain feed into HarfangLab
description: |
  Downloads a plain-text feed of malicious domains every hour, keeps the
  domains in the `threat-domains` lookup table for enrichment, and
  synchronizes them into the HarfangLab IOC source `tenzir-threat-domains`.
  Domains that leave the feed are disabled in HarfangLab.

  Declare the lookup table in the configuration as
  `contexts/threat-domains.yaml` with `type: lookup-table`. For a large feed,
  import it into the source once with the Manager's CSV import; the hourly
  runs then only write the differences.
---

every 1h {
  from_http "https://feeds.example.org/malicious-domains.txt" {
    read_lines
  }
  where line != "" and not line.starts_with("#")
  this = {domain: line}
  fork {
    context_update "threat-domains", key=domain
  }
  harfanglab::ioc::sync "https://example.hurukai.io:8443",
    token=secret("harfanglab-api-token"),
    source="tenzir-threat-domains",
    type="domain",
    value=domain,
    prune=true
}
